    "retention": {
      "office_mid": "partially_preserved",
      "office_pano": "fully_preserved"
    },
    "summary": "The manager narrows it down to one person, staring across the desk; she denies it flatly and without heat.",
    "shots": "Entry state, re-anchored to the reference image: 钱经理 (S3) is leaning on the far side of the desk with one palm flat on it, the grey filing cabinets directly behind him, facing the camera; 苏小满 (S1) stands at the near side of the desk with her back to the camera and a plain stretch of white wall behind her, facing him. The closed wooden door in the back wall stays shut and its surface is plain wood.\n[Shot 1] Medium over the desk: 钱经理 (S3) straightens up slowly, tucks both hands behind his back and tips his head to one side, fixing her with the look of a man who has already decided, and speaks in a flat accusing Mandarin, one phrase at a time: [Chinese] 收台的时候，就你一个人在。\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.600, reverse single on 苏小满 (S1) on the near side of the desk, the blind-light barring the wall behind her; she does not move her feet and does not look away, and answers at once in a low steady Mandarin: [Chinese] 不是我。\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.800, wide shot across the desk: he stands behind it facing the lens, she stands at the near end with her back to the lens, the grey filing cabinets fill the wall behind him and a plain stretch of white wall with a band of blind-light fills the wall behind her, and the whole room stays very still.\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.200, the camera creeps a few centimetres closer on the desk surface between them. Neither of them speaks.",
    "soundscape": "A clock ticking on the wall, the low hum of the ceiling lights, one nervous swallow, a faint breath of room tone from the ceiling lights.",
    "music": "N/A",
    "crowd": false,
    "style_pack": "lean",
    "_lean_shots": "[Shot 1] Medium over the desk: 钱经理 (S3) straightens up slowly, tucks both hands behind his back and tips his head to one side, fixing her with the look of a man who has already decided, and speaks in a flat accusing Mandarin, one phrase at a time: [Chinese] 收台的时候，就你一个人在。\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.600, reverse single on 苏小满 (S1) on the near side of the desk, the blind-light barring the wall behind her; she does not move her feet and does not look away, and answers at once in a low steady Mandarin: [Chinese] 不是我。\n[Shot 3] At 00:07.800, wide two-shot across the desk, both of them motionless at either side of it, the room very still, the two of them alone in the frame with clear empty space behind each of them.\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.200, the camera creeps a few centimetres closer on the desk surface between them. Neither of them speaks.",
    "lean_anchor": "The whole clip takes place in one small private office and the camera never leaves it. The room has four plain white walls, a grey metal filing cabinet along the far wall, a long wooden desk standing across the middle of the floor, and venetian blinds on the right-hand wall laying bright bands of light across the desk top and the floor. A closed wooden door is set flat into the back wall, its surface plain wood with a small silver handle. Everything in this room reads as an office interior: the desk, the cabinet, the blinds and the plain painted walls. The office is one small private room: a wooden desk stands across the middle of it, long side to the camera, and behind that desk the wall is covered with grey metal filing cabinets. Bright mid-morning daylight comes through venetian blinds on the right-hand wall and lays bright bands across the desk top and the floor. The people named in this beat are the only people in it: the manager stays behind the desk on the far side and the cleaner stays at the near end with her back to the camera. 钱经理 (S3), the manager, is a stocky middle-aged man in a white shirt and charcoal waistcoat; he stays on the far side of that desk for the entire clip, standing behind it with the filing cabinets directly behind his back, facing the camera, his weight on the desk. 苏小满 (S1), the cleaner, is a young woman in a navy work shirt with a grey apron; she stays on the near side of that desk for the entire clip, standing with her back to the camera and a plain stretch of white wall behind her, facing him. The camera stands on the near side of the desk and looks across it at him, so he is further away and smaller, and she is closer to the lens with her back turned. The room around them is plain and bright: white walls, a band of venetian-blind light on the right-hand wall, a closed wooden door set flat into the back wall, and the desk between them clear except a single sheet of paper and one pen lying flat near its middle."
  },
  {
